Z||000000||ITA_FIERO||02-02-2000||10:24 PM||||Once upon a time there was a guy that lusted after a military dictator's daughter.  Well, one night he um..."made love" to this girl and the father (a general) vowed to track him down and kill him.  The poor kid spent the next 3 years fleaing from continent to continent, literally leaping from stone to stone and hiding in bushes, with the general never more than a day behind.  One day outside of Baghdad, Romeo was so cold and tired that he hid in a Ziggurat (an ancient Babylonian temple) and built a small fire to warm himself.  The angry father saw the smoke, swarmed the ziggurat and killed the lover boy.<BR>The Moral:  The searching general has proven that a smoking ziggurat is bad for one's stealth.||||reg||1
